{"duration": 54.269, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A naval officer hoisted a massive lantern atop a rusted pole.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.785}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He balanced the weight, sweat dripping, while the sea roared.", "start": 4.005, "end": 6.738}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His crew laughed, saying a tower would never change the storm.", "start": 7.158, "end": 10.137}, {"beat": 1, "text": "They muttered that a wooden pier could do the job.", "start": 10.357, "end": 12.725}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The government orders the tower\u2019s steel skeleton to rise in 1910.", "start": 13.145, "end": 17.021}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Engineers sketch blueprints on cramped desks.", "start": 17.241, "end": 19.518}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Workers weld the frame while ships wait for safe passage.", "start": 19.738, "end": 22.728}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Every night the unfinished tower glints in fog.", "start": 22.948, "end": 25.221}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like putting a bright sign on a dark road you travel every day.", "start": 25.641, "end": 29.279}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The real reason: the state needed a high\u2011point to record weather.", "start": 29.699, "end": 32.98}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The lighthouse would measure wind, rain, and tides for the port.", "start": 33.2, "end": 36.307}, {"beat": 4, "text": "At the same time it broadcast a glowing symbol of modern Japan.", "start": 36.527, "end": 40.096}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Foreign visitors would see the flash and think Japan was advanced.", "start": 40.316, "end": 43.542}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the lighthouse\u2019s flash later guided not only ships, but also the nation\u2019s own propaganda ships.", "start": 43.962, "end": 50.238}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The tower became a beacon for both safety and pride.", "start": 50.458, "end": 53.149}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.124, "end": 0.174, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "naval", "start": 0.224, "end": 0.524, "line": 0